    "result": "Perfect! All tests are passing. Here's a summary of the fixes I made:\n\n## Summary\n\nI fixed two failing tests in the frai-core test suite:\n\n### 1. **Finetune governance test** (`src/finetune/governance.test.js:152`)\n**Problem**: The test tried to import `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export but it was only available in the default export.\n\n**Fix**: Added named exports in `src/finetune/index.js` after the schema imports:\n```javascript\nexport { APPROVAL_STATUSES, DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS, GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS, RISK_LEVELS };\n```\n\n### 2. **Evaluation toxicity test** (`src/eval/index.test.js:48`)\n**Problem**: The `toxicityMetric` function had `bannedTerms` as its second parameter, but `runEvaluations` calls all metrics with `(outputs, references)`. This caused the references array to be treated as banned terms, incorrectly flagging safe outputs.\n\n**Fix**: Changed the function signature in `src/eval/metrics.js` to accept `references` instead of `bannedTerms`:\n```javascript\nexport function toxicityMetric(outputs, references) {\n  // Now uses defaultBannedTerms instead of the second parameter\n  const terms = defaultBannedTerms.map((term) => term.toLowerCase());\n  // ... rest of implementation\n}\n```\n\n**Result**: All 28 tests across 8 test files now pass \u2705",
